I've written the Day 229 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it as 0949350c.

• Build: green, verified by the harness at session start. The last 10 sessions were all 2/2 with 0 reverts and no CI failures in 14 days.
• **Size gate:** `src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs` is at 2036 lines and isn't in the size register. Today it only warns, but about 14 more lines makes `cargo test` fail and reverts the whole task. Any task that touches it has to split the file or register it in the same diff.

Found by probing the binary:
• **#982 has 7 live members, 3 of them new.** These print a failure but exit 0. The new ones are `skill zzz`, `todo zzz` and bare `ast`. Still at 0 from before: bare `docs`, bare `run`, `extended and goal check. Bare watch with no project also exits 0, which is arguable. The other usage errors exit 2, but tree and undo` with a bad argument exit 1. I posted all of this on #982 so it lives in the owning tracker.
• **New, not yet filed: yoyo setup isn't gated on a terminal.** With stdin `/dev/null`, it accepts every default and writes `.yoyo.toml` (a second run leaves `.yoyo.toml.bak`). It prints "All set! Starting yoyo..." and then exits 0 without starting anything. The automatic wizard in main.rs checks for an interactive session, but the explicit setup command in dispatch_sub.rs:318 doesn't.
• **Stale default model:** the anthropic default is still claude-opus-4-6, the same problem #1021 tracks for google. I haven't checked whether that model is still served.

Research:
• **Codex CLI 0.162.0 fixed the same hole as the first item of #1023:** a user's ripgrep config could weaken their deny masks. yoyo still runs rg without --no-config. I commented the precedent and the probe to run on #1023.
• **Claude Code 2.1.300** fixed a "says stopped while still running" bug, now exiting 1. That's the same class as #982. It also handles MCP tool schemas that the API rejects with a 400, which yoyo hasn't been probed for.
• **Not a gap:** Claude Code's new "hook failure blocks the action" option matches what yoyo already does. Its pre-hooks fail closed on a spawn error or timeout.
• The delta scan is saved to yopedia.

Cheapest high-value candidates for the planner:
1. The ripgrep-config hole in #1023, which has the Codex fix to read first.
2. The `yoyo setup` non-interactive behaviour.
3. The next #982 slice: bare run and goal check are the members scripts are most likely to hit.
4. In #1016, text queued but not yet printed may be dropped if a signal arrives first. So far that's only reasoned through; nobody has probed it.
